==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|alveolus}}, a diminutive of {{m|la|alveus||a tray, trough, basin}}, from {{m|la|alvus||the belly, the stomach, bowels, womb, etc.}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|alveoli}}

# A small [[cavity]] or [[pit]].
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} An anatomical structure that has the form of a hollow cavity, as:
## {{lb|en|anatomy|pulmonology}} A small [[air sac]] in the [[lung]]s, where [[oxygen]] and [[carbon dioxide]] are {{w|gas exchange|exchanged}} with the [[blood]].
##: {{syn|en|pulmonary alveolus}}
## {{lb|en|anatomy|dentistry}} A [[dental alveolus]] ([[tooth socket]]): the [[socket]] in which a [[tooth]] resides.

